  faqs: [
    { question: "Is there an IB or IGCSE school in Mattannur?", answer: "Not that we could confirm. No school listed for the town is shown as an IB World School or a Cambridge centre, so we name none. The nearest confirmed Cambridge school is GEM International School in Kannur city, and Kochi offers Kerala's widest choice. If a confirmed school turns up in Mattannur, we will correct this page." },
    { question: "Will a tutor visit our house in Mattannur?", answer: "No. Our tutors teach in person only in Gurugram and parts of Delhi NCR. Mattannur lessons are live over video with a shared whiteboard, and your child works in their own room at an agreed hour, so the calm of home tuition stays while nobody has to travel along the Coorg road." },
    { question: "How do we get started?", answer: "Email support@ibgram.com or WhatsApp +91 7439 368 115 with the programme or board, the subject and level, the latest marks and the times that suit the family. We reply with a short list of matched tutors, and one of them teaches your child a free trial lesson." },
    { question: "What decides the fee for a Mattannur student?", answer: "Four things: the course and level, how often lessons run, the tutor's recent work on the exact specification and how near the exam is. We publish no price list, yet you receive a written quote before booking. Nothing is added for distance because every lesson is online, and the trial lesson costs nothing." },
    { question: "Is the first lesson really free?", answer: "Yes. Each match opens with a complete trial lesson on genuine syllabus material and a brief note afterwards. If the tutor is not right, we suggest another or stop there, with nothing owed. Parents are welcome to listen in to see how their child responds." },
    { question: "Can a tutor write my child's IA or Extended Essay?", answer: "No. Tutors never write a student's IA, Extended Essay, TOK essay or coursework, and they do not polish drafts into finished work. They explain the criteria, help narrow a question, comment on a plan and mark practice pieces, while the submitted text stays entirely the student's, as the IB and the exam boards insist." },
    { question: "Which Diploma subjects can you cover?", answer: "Most of the common ones: both Maths courses, Physics, Chemistry, Biology, Economics, Business Management, English A, Computer Science and Psychology, plus Malayalam A and Hindi B. For something less usual, such as Theatre or Geography, ask us first and we will confirm a suitable tutor before you commit." },
    { question: "Our child studies in the Gulf. Can lessons still work?", answer: "Yes, because lessons follow Indian Standard Time and most Gulf countries run one and a half to two and a half hours behind it. Tutor and student fix a slot that fits the Gulf school day, and the same tutor can continue during summer weeks in Mattannur and term time abroad." },
    { question: "We attend a Cambridge school in Kannur city. Is extra tuition useful?", answer: "It often is. A specialist can re-explain Extended Mathematics, Physics or Chemistry in a different way, time past papers with the student or prepare a retake. The tutor follows the school's syllabus code and tier and supports classroom teaching rather than competing with it." },
    { question: "Do you teach younger children in MYP and PYP?", answer: "Yes, with the same care. In MYP the work is usually writing to criteria and pacing the Personal Project; in PYP it is reading, number sense and the habit of asking questions. Younger children generally learn best in shorter, regular sessions." },
    { question: "Is it realistic to move from the Kerala syllabus or CBSE to IGCSE?", answer: "Yes, provided exam technique is taught from the start. Much of the content will be familiar, but IGCSE papers reward method, command words and reasoning on questions the student has not seen. Early sessions focus on those habits and on picking a tier, so the change feels like a new style, not a fresh start." },
    { question: "What happens if heavy rain or a power cut interrupts a lesson?", answer: "We move it. If video drops, the tutor can continue by voice, and a missed session is rebooked. During the wettest weeks we suggest agreeing a standby time for important lessons, and a charged laptop or a mobile hotspot is a cheap safeguard." },
    { question: "How are tutors chosen and checked?", answer: "We look at qualifications, recent teaching of the exact subject and level, and how the person explains a live topic in a short demonstration. You see the background before you choose, and the free lesson shows the teaching style first-hand." },
    { question: "When should tutoring begin?", answer: "Early: Grade 9 for IGCSE and Class 11 for the Diploma. Even eight to twelve weeks before a mock helps, and starting late is better than not starting. The tutor sets goals that suit the time left." },
    { question: "Can my child sit IGCSE as a private candidate from Mattannur?", answer: "Possibly. A private candidate needs an approved centre that accepts outside entries and must register months ahead of the series. Tutors can plan the study timetable, but the family confirms the centre and entry deadlines directly with the exam board or the centre." },
    { question: "Does IB Gram have any link with a school, board or university?", answer: "No. IB Gram is an independent service. It is not connected to GEM International School or any other school named on this page, to the International Baccalaureate Organization, to Cambridge Assessment International Education or to Pearson Edexcel. Schools are named only so Mattannur families see an honest local picture." },
  ],

